Main operational document that groups one or more stock moves for a complete warehouse process — Incoming Receipt, Customer Delivery, Internal Transfer, Manufacturing, etc.
Key Functional Use Cases:

Supplier Receipts (from Purchase Orders)
Customer Deliveries (from Sales Orders)
Internal transfers between locations/warehouses
Manufacturing component consumption & finished goods receipt
Returns, scrap, inventory adjustments
Batch picking, wave picking, and put-away
Multi-step operations (2-step / 3-step receipt/delivery)

Technical DNA:

Model Type: models.Model (persistent + mail.thread + activity.mixin)
Key Fields:
name (sequenced: WH/OUT/xxxx, WH/IN/xxxx), picking_type_id → stock.picking.type
state (draft/confirmed/assigned/done/cancel)
partner_id, scheduled_date, date_done
origin (SO/PO reference), group_id
One2many: move_ids → stock.move (main child)
One2many: move_line_ids → stock.move.line
location_id, location_dest_id
backorder_id, return_id

Critical Hooks: action_confirm, action_assign, button_validate, _action_done, action_generate_backorder
Security: stock.group_stock_user + picking type + location rules

RAG Routing Keywords:
stock picking, warehouse picking, delivery order, goods receipt, incoming shipment, outgoing shipment, internal transfer, stock operation, picking document, WH/IN, WH/OUT, picking list, validate picking, pending delivery, ready to transfer, waiting availability, not yet delivered, undelivered, backorder, shipped, done transfer, draft transfer, cancelled picking, late delivery, picking status
Related Models (most joined):

stock.picking.type (operation type)
stock.move (main lines)
stock.move.line (detailed lots)
sale.order / purchase.order (origin)
res.partner
stock.warehouse, stock.location
stock.quant

Ultra-Dense Vector Paragraph:
stock.picking is Odoo’s main warehouse document model representing a complete picking operation (receipt, delivery, internal transfer) with picking_type_id, move_ids, move_line_ids, state, and scheduled_date. It groups stock moves, controls validation, reservations, backorders, and serves as the operational bridge between Sales, Purchase, Manufacturing, and Inventory modules.